it may be something for the history, why they decided at a certain time in history to say Berakha, and everything,

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:17.000
Now, there is a theory, although there is no Pasuk, there is a theory, and what is the theory?

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:24.000
We studied this last week, that the whole world belongs to God, and therefore, the whole world is a temple,

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:30.000
because what was seen, what the Talmud does here, since it is a Sevarah, there is no Pasuk,

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:40.000
to give you, use categories, that are easy for you to grasp, and that you will immediately accept,

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:51.000
and one thing that was common for the ancient man, a Jew, a non-Jew, but the non-Jew was even more common for him than the Jew,

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:58.000
is that the worst sin that you could conceive, worse than raping, this, raping, but nothing,

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:06.000
the worst sin is sacrilege, what is sacrilege? To use something that was consecrated to the temple,

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:13.000
give you an example, if you want to say today something about the senator, he did some other one,

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:20.000
so you probably know, he is a pedophile, in antiquity you don't say he is a pedophile,

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:27.000
you say like this, that he was walking through the gardens of such and such a god,

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:36.000
and you saw him breaking a branch, that is the worst thing you could say about a human being,

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:46.000
because he had Hanakah, from that branch, just by cutting it to a leaf of a consecrated tree,

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:52.000
this is the worst thing you could say about anybody, all right?

00:11:52.000 --> 00:12:02.000
So, here come the Hachamim, in the business of the Pasuk, they point out to you that the whole world belongs to God,

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:10.000
Labonai ha-ares omloa, to God the whole world belongs, if the whole world belongs to God,

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:17.000
then again, applying the logic of the ancient man, if you take it,

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:24.000
kol ha-minim ha-olam ha-zeh, ma'al, it should make you feel like a man, the whole world belongs to God,

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:32.000
so it says, ah, the Pasuk says, Labonai ha-ares omloa, there is another Pasuk says,

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:40.000
ha-ares matatidim mi-adam, ha-kesak, if never a Hanak is ma'al, the whole world belongs to God,

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:46.000
but if you acknowledge, in a minute I say, in a minute I say what you acknowledge,

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:53.000
then, he is, the world belongs to you, what you acknowledge, what you have to acknowledge,

00:12:53.000 --> 00:13:01.000
is a very important thing, melek ha-olam, in berkhot ha-nenim, in this berakhot, you say melek ha-olam,

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:07.000
in the berakhot of ha-tefilah, you say, elohenu, elabatenu, elaburham, elisahu, elakoh, you say melek ha-olam,

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:14.000
marfat ta-shem melek ha-olam el-hayya matim, you don't say this, or marfat ta-shem melek ha-olam el-kha-nena da'at,

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:20.000
you don't say this, why not, because nothing to do with olam ha-zeh directly, you are there,

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:27.000
you are praising God as he is, here I am taking something from him, and therefore before I take it,

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:33.000
I say, I acknowledge that you are the master of this thing, so here there is a very important thing,

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:40.000
I discussed this in a paper of mine, I wrote, I published, that according to the gemara, the peshat,

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:47.000
although the halonim and so on, they all come to people, but the peshat is, that if you say a berakhot,

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:57.000
berkhot ha-nenim, and you skip melek ha-olam, marfat ta-shem koreferi ha-adama, you skip melek ha-olam,

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:11.000
so I think that this is important, because the concept is of, he is the boss, there is a very beautiful word in English,

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:17.000
that is used by Newton, and I have mentioned this in my article in connection to all this type of things,

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:25.000
which is dominion of God, and the word dominion comes from the word dominos, which means the Lord,

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:34.000
you see, you understand, he is the dominion of God's dominion, because he is the dominos, he is the Lord of the world,

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:40.000
yes, of course I claim that he took this from haram bam, the gemara, as I told you about Isaac Newton,

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:49.000
and so the question is acknowledging God's dominion on earth, and this we acknowledge, God's dominion,

00:14:49.000 --> 00:15:00.000
by saying melek ha-olam, he is the master of the universe, simple, so you have a concept, because it is a concept,

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:08.000
and you don't have a pasuk, it is only a sevara, if you want it to be more than sevara, you quote me the pasuk,

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:14.000
unfortunately there is no pasuk, the tribe, last week, and the yeshiva failed,

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:28.000
now it is the same thing done by different schools, of the same thing about what we did before,

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:41.000
about the first, and then the other says, he says, and the other says,

