you understand the question, the tension between the ganeka, which is parallel to the question, to the tension,

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:11.000
the same tension, is it God or is it yours, who is the dominion here, right?

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:33.000
Lakashia, if you are an adulteress, then it is yours, when you acknowledge that this is God, God gives it to you,

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:45.000
if you don't acknowledge that he is the dominions, yes, or the alone of this world, then it is not yours, just a second,

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:57.000
there is a problem, which I think I was able to solve, the problem is, and the following,

00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:13.000
Harambam counts, believe in God, as one of the miswot, so, a very sharp minded rabbi in Spain, Rabbi Hazzai Crescas,

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:25.000
he said, no, this cannot be a miswot, because before you believe in God as a miswot,

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:31.000
miswot is a person who is a commander, somebody who orders things, you understand,

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:38.000
now, before I am the miswot of believing in God, I have to believe that there is somebody who commands me this,

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:48.000
but if I believe in that already, I believe, I fulfill the miswot, so, how do you believe there is a miswot of believing in God,

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:54.000
before you fulfill the miswot, you have to believe that there is somebody who commands you,

00:18:54.000 --> 00:19:03.000
how do you believe in God, so, what is the point, a very good question, nobody was able to answer except me,

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:12.000
I have two answers, one is a sophisticated one, philosophical, and I don't want to do this, I did this in my union,

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:23.000
and the other one, which is a legal one, for an ambam, if I say I believe in God, there is a God created of Shammai and Ba'aretz,

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:28.000
blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, it doesn't count for a miswot,

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:36.000
the miswot is when you acknowledge that he has dominion over the earth,

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:46.000
for an ambam, the miswot of believing in God, is not to believe in an abstract God, who created Shammai and Ba'aretz,

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:54.000
but in a God that created Shammai and Ba'aretz, and he has dominion on this planet,

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:59.000
his acknowledgement of his dominion,

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:10.000
there is Hashem, that's not enough,

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:20.000
the miswot of believing in God, is not in the first part of the Barakah,

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:27.000
but that God has dominion on earth,

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:35.000
understand, I bring this from, by reading carefully, the ambam refers about this miswot in two places,

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:39.000
in three places, but one in Hebrew, in the Mishneh Torah,

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:44.000
so there you could, if you don't know Hebrew well, you could make the mistake that Rabbi Hazarik Reskas makes,

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:52.000
but in the Arabic, it's impossible, I mean, if you know the Arabic, you cannot make the mistake,

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:57.000
Rabbubieh, Rabbubieh means dominion,

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:02.000
the miswot is dominion of God over the earth,

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:06.000
all right,

