00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:09.000
argued that,

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:10.000
the Jews,

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:12.000
the Peshat is a very,

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:14.000
it's post Talmudic,

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:15.000
before in the Talmud time,

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:17.000
there was no notion of Peshat,

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:18.000
that's what he says,

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:21.000
and I believe he is not correct,

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:22.000
and,

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:23.000
and many,

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:25.000
I believe that there are many words,

00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:26.000
with the equivalent of Peshat,

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:27.000
one of them is,

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:28.000
debarim kichtavam,

00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:32.000
yahol debarim kichtavam,

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:34.000
now,

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:35.000
could it be that,

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:37.000
loyamos sefer ha-Torah ha-Zemepicha,

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:38.000
is kichtavo,

00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:40.000
it's literally so,

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:43.000
never stop reading the Torah,

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:44.000
yes,

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:45.000
yes,

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:46.000
continue.

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:47.000
In the Talmud,

00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:48.000
loyamos sefer ha-Torah ha-Zemepicha,

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:50.000
be-asafta de-ganekha,

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:52.000
now the Torah says also,

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:53.000
be-asafta de-ganekha,

00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:55.000
so therefore,

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:56.000
the Pasuk,

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:58.000
loyamos sefer ha-Torah ha-Zemepicha,

00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:01.000
cannot be kichtavo,

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:04.000
because the Torah says,

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:06.000
be-asafta de-ganekha,

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:07.000
be-asafta de-ganekha,

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:09.000
go and harvest your planting,

00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:10.000
whatever it is,

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:11.000
you're great.

00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:14.000
This means that the Torah is telling you,

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:16.000
go on and work.

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:19.000
Ah,

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:20.000
the Pasuk says,

00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:21.000
loyamos sefer ha-Torah ha-Zemepicha,

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:22.000
how do you go to work?

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:24.000
So,

00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:26.000
han-heg bah-hen min-ha,

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:27.000
tere-chere,

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:28.000
han-heg min-ha,

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:29.000
tere-chere,

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:30.000
tere-chere,

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.000
tere-chere,

00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:32.000
tere-chere,

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:33.000
tere-chere,

00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:34.000
tere-chere,

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.000
han-heg min-ha,

00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:37.000
bah-hen min-ha,

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:38.000
tere-chere.

00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:39.000
Very beautiful answer.

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:41.000
We have a tension.

00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:45.000
One place says,

00:25:46.000 --> 00:25:47.000
work.

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:50.000
The other place says,

00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:52.000
study.

00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:55.000
Han-heg bah-hen min-ha,

00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:56.000
tere-chere.

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:58.000
You have to accommodate both

00:25:58.000 --> 00:25:59.000
at the same time.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.000
And then we're going to have illustrations.

00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:03.000
What does that mean?

00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:05.000
Yes, you study,

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:07.000
but you also work.

00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:09.000
Yes, you work,

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:10.000
but you also study.

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:12.000
Han-heg bah-hen min-ha,

00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:13.000
tere-chere.

00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:14.000
It means you have to accommodate

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:15.000
both of them

00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:17.000
according to the circumstances

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:19.000
of your tere-chere.

00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:20.000
According to us,

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:21.000
you walk on earth.

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:23.000
According to the circumstances.

00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:25.000
You must accommodate them

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:27.000
according to circumstances.

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:29.000
You study the whole day,

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:31.000
and you work the whole day.

00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:33.000
How do you do this?

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:34.000
You accommodate this.

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:36.000
Right?

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:37.000
You have two agendas.

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:39.000
And according to circumstances,

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:41.000
we're going to have concrete examples.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:43.000
You're going to

00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:45.000
accommodate the agenda.

00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:46.000
All right?

00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:47.000
Fine.

00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:52.000
This is the position

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:53.000
of Rabbi Ishmael.

00:26:57.000 --> 00:26:58.000
No, Rabbi Yohai

00:26:58.000 --> 00:26:59.000
