00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:05.000
Anybody wants to...

00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:07.000
The beginning of the Sugayimim?

00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:08.000
Yes.

00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:09.000
You remember it?

00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:10.000
Yeah.

00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:11.000
How?

00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:13.000
I looked at it just now.

00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:15.000
I didn't write it down.

00:35:15.000 --> 00:35:17.000
All right. Just let me hear it.

00:35:17.000 --> 00:35:19.000
There's...

00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:21.000
a tension created by two verses.

00:35:21.000 --> 00:35:23.000
One verse says...

00:35:23.000 --> 00:35:25.000
One verse says that...

00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:27.000
that one should always be involved

00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:28.000
in studying Baha'u'llah.

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:29.000
Yes.

00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:31.000
Another verse says...

00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:33.000
that you should go out into the field

00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:36.000
and harvest the wheat.

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.000
So it seems...

00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:39.000
it seems contradictory in the sense that...

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:40.000
It is contradictory,

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:42.000
because, as you see,

00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:43.000
first of all,

00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:45.000
we want to have the history of the Sugayimim.

00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:47.000
The history of the Sugayimim is very important.

00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:49.000
The history of the Sugayimim.

00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:52.000
We are dealing with a concept.

00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:54.000
The concept is of Berachah,

00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:55.000
or saying blessings.

00:35:55.000 --> 00:35:56.000
Koran 8,

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:57.000
in the HaOlam HaZeh,

00:35:57.000 --> 00:35:58.000
Berachah Ma'al,

00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:00.000
in the Mishnah,

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.000
that says,

00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:03.000
Kesad Me'valikim Ha'la Perot.

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:04.000
This is the chapter.

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:07.000
We have to say blessings on food.

00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:08.000
The question is,

00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:11.000
it assumes that there is a source of obligation.

00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:14.000
What is the source of this obligation?

00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:15.000
In the first Sugayimim,

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:17.000
we establish one thing.

00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:19.000
There is no basuk.

00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:21.000
There is absolutely no verse for it.

00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:23.000
If there is no verse,

00:36:23.000 --> 00:36:24.000
then,

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:27.000
and there is no verse that you could even connect it,

00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:28.000
yes,

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:30.000
there is no verse,

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:32.000
then you know two things.

00:36:32.000 --> 00:36:33.000
Number one,

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:34.000
you know,

00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:35.000
is Sebarah.

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:36.000
Sebarah means,

00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:37.000
a theory.

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:39.000
A theory in Jewish law

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:41.000
is the lowest of all sources.

00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:42.000
Yes,

00:36:42.000 --> 00:36:43.000
it's a theory,

00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:44.000
an opinion.

00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:45.000
All right?

00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:46.000
And that's an opinion,

00:36:46.000 --> 00:36:47.000
and therefore,

00:36:47.000 --> 00:36:48.000
when we say there is a Sebarah,

00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:50.000
it means I have absolutely no proofs.

00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:52.000
Sebarah means no proofs,

00:36:52.000 --> 00:36:53.000
no legal proofs.

00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:55.000
That's number one.

00:36:55.000 --> 00:36:58.000
Because it's a Sebarah,

00:36:58.000 --> 00:37:01.000
you must develop the concept.

00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:03.000
So one thing we start establishing

00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:04.000
in the preceding Sugayimim,

00:37:04.000 --> 00:37:05.000
Sebarah,

00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:10.000
means there are no verses to this idea.

00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:11.000
Now,

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:12.000
we have to develop,

00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:16.000
if it has no sources in the Torah,

00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:18.000
it is a concept.

00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:21.000
What is the concept?

00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:22.000
So now,

00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:26.000
we've got two Pesukim.

00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:28.000
Da'lunai ha'alez umlo'ah.

00:37:28.000 --> 00:37:30.000
That is one.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:31.000
And the other is what?

00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:34.000
Ve'ha'alez natan nebne'adam.

00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:35.000
All right?

00:37:35.000 --> 00:37:36.000
So,

00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:37.000
is it God's,

00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:38.000
the earth,

00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:41.000
or is it nebne'adam?

00:37:41.000 --> 00:37:43.000
Kar nefne'berakah,

00:37:43.000 --> 00:37:45.000
kar nefne'ahar-e-berakah.

00:37:45.000 --> 00:37:46.000
Now,

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:48.000
since we're talking about this,

00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:49.000
how would you say,

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:50.000
the whole notion of

00:37:50.000 --> 00:37:51.000
Da'lunai ha'alez umlo'ah,

00:37:51.000 --> 00:37:53.000
what does it mean?

00:37:53.000 --> 00:37:54.000
Let's see,

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:55.000
any of you.

00:37:55.000 --> 00:37:56.000
Let's see,

00:37:56.000 --> 00:37:57.000
Amy.

00:37:57.000 --> 00:37:59.000
What does it mean?

00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:01.000
It means that you recognize that God

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:03.000
is the king in this world.

00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:04.000
Dominion.

00:38:04.000 --> 00:38:05.000
Dominion.

00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:06.000
It's called dominion.

00:38:06.000 --> 00:38:09.000
God has dominion over the earth.

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:12.000
Dominion.

00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:13.000
All right.

00:38:13.000 --> 00:38:14.000
What does it mean that

00:38:14.000 --> 00:38:16.000
God created the universe?

00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:18.000
It's not only a metaphysical concept.

00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:19.000
It is,

00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:21.000
God has dominion.

00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:22.000
Yes.

00:38:22.000 --> 00:38:23.000
As I'm talking in Hebrew,

00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:24.000
to create,

00:38:24.000 --> 00:38:25.000
and to own,

00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:28.000
is the same word.

00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:30.000
Kaniti ish et ha'Elohim.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:31.000
What does it mean,

00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:32.000
kaniti?

00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:34.000
I shaped.

00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:35.000
Havar,

00:38:35.000 --> 00:38:36.000
when the first time she had a child,

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:37.000
she said,

00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:39.000
kaniti ish et ha'Elohim.

00:38:39.000 --> 00:38:40.000
What does it mean?

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:41.000
Kosm kai.

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:42.000
Kaniti,

00:38:42.000 --> 00:38:43.000
what does it mean,

00:38:43.000 --> 00:38:45.000
a human together with God.

00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:46.000
God and me,

00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:47.000
together we shape.

00:38:47.000 --> 00:38:49.000
Konei shamai va'arez.

00:38:49.000 --> 00:38:50.000
Pardon me.

00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:51.000
He shapes,

00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:52.000
shamai va'arez.

00:38:52.000 --> 00:38:53.000
He creates,

00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:54.000
he owns.

00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:55.000
All right.

00:38:55.000 --> 00:38:56.000
Dominion.

00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:57.000
So,

00:38:57.000 --> 00:38:58.000
la'adonai ha'arez umloa.

00:38:58.000 --> 00:38:59.000
Now,

00:38:59.000 --> 00:39:01.000
if the whole world belongs to God,

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:03.000
then,

00:39:03.000 --> 00:39:05.000
chakush ha'avei ni'ana,

00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:07.000
kanif ne'berachat,

00:39:07.000 --> 00:39:08.000
kan yachararecha.

00:39:08.000 --> 00:39:09.000
What you do in the berachat,

00:39:09.000 --> 00:39:12.000
you acknowledge that he has dominion.

00:39:12.000 --> 00:39:13.000
Baruch atah,

00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:14.000
Hashem,

00:39:14.000 --> 00:39:15.000
melek ha'olam.

00:39:15.000 --> 00:39:17.000
Dominion over the earth.

00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:18.000
All right.

00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:19.000
He's like a dominion.

00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:21.000
Once that you recognize that he has dominion,

00:39:21.000 --> 00:39:22.000
then,

00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:23.000
is,

00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:24.000
uh,

00:39:24.000 --> 00:39:25.000
you know,

00:39:25.000 --> 00:39:27.000
it belongs to you.

00:39:27.000 --> 00:39:28.000
He gives it to you.

00:39:28.000 --> 00:39:29.000
Otherwise,

00:39:29.000 --> 00:39:30.000
ma'ad,

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:31.000
tension between

00:39:31.000 --> 00:39:32.000
dominion

00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:33.000
and ha'arez.

00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:34.000
Now,

00:39:34.000 --> 00:39:35.000
I said,

00:39:35.000 --> 00:39:36.000
I made a parenthesis,

00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:37.000
because we're reviewing.

00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:38.000
And it says,

00:39:38.000 --> 00:39:39.000
this answers a very difficult question

00:39:39.000 --> 00:39:40.000
on Arambam.

00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:41.000
Maybe Maurice,

00:39:41.000 --> 00:39:42.000
you want to say it.

00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:43.000
Maurice,

00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:44.000
you want to say the question on Arambam.

00:39:44.000 --> 00:39:45.000
Or you want,

00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:46.000
whatever it is,

00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:47.000
whatever it is.

00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:48.000
Chazdai Kreskas,

00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:49.000
I think,

00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:50.000
asked the question.

00:39:50.000 --> 00:39:51.000
Yeah.

00:39:51.000 --> 00:39:52.000
Arambam counts

00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:53.000
believing God

00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:54.000
as a misbah.

00:39:54.000 --> 00:39:55.000
The first misbah

00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:56.000
is to believe in God.

00:39:56.000 --> 00:39:57.000
All right.

00:39:57.000 --> 00:39:58.000
So,

00:39:58.000 --> 00:39:59.000
Chazdai Kreskas

00:39:59.000 --> 00:40:00.000
asked a question.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:01.000
What is the question he asked?

00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:02.000
Uh,

00:40:02.000 --> 00:40:03.000
the fact that you believe

00:40:03.000 --> 00:40:04.000
that you,

00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:05.000
uh,

00:40:05.000 --> 00:40:06.000
if there's a,

00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:07.000
if you,

00:40:07.000 --> 00:40:08.000
if you accept the commandment,

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:09.000
this presupposes that...

00:40:09.000 --> 00:40:10.000
I mean,

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:11.000
this presupposes that is what?

00:40:11.000 --> 00:40:12.000
Commandment.

00:40:12.000 --> 00:40:13.000
A misbah.

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:14.000
I mean,

00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:15.000
a commandment.

00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:16.000
So now,

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:17.000
before you make,

00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:18.000
you make a misbah,

00:40:18.000 --> 00:40:19.000
you already,

00:40:19.000 --> 00:40:20.000
you believe in God.

00:40:20.000 --> 00:40:21.000
So,

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:22.000
I believe in God

00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:23.000
because God told me.

00:40:23.000 --> 00:40:24.000
I mean,

00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:25.000
you will,

00:40:25.000 --> 00:40:26.000
misbah.

00:40:26.000 --> 00:40:27.000
This is a misbah,

00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:28.000
yes?

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:29.000
If there is a misbah,

00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:30.000
means that God is,

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.000
to be a misbah,

00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:32.000
has to be a misbah.

00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:33.000
So,

00:40:33.000 --> 00:40:34.000
you already believe in God.

00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:35.000
You have to believe

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:36.000
in the misbah.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:37.000
So,

00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:38.000
what,

00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:39.000
how could it be a misbah

00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:40.000
to,

00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:41.000
to,

00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:42.000
to believe in God?

00:40:42.000 --> 00:40:43.000
Is that a problem?

00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:44.000
So,

00:40:44.000 --> 00:40:45.000
what was,

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:46.000
what?

00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:47.000
Yeah.

00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:48.000
So,

00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:49.000
so,

00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:50.000
therefore,

00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:51.000
here I have to,

00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:52.000
to presuppose that before you believe in God,

00:40:52.000 --> 00:40:53.000
you believe in somebody

00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:54.000
who commanded you to believe in God.

00:40:54.000 --> 00:40:55.000
But that somebody

00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:56.000
must be God.

00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:57.000
Only God can command you.

00:40:57.000 --> 00:40:58.000
So,

00:40:58.000 --> 00:40:59.000
you believe in it.

00:40:59.000 --> 00:41:00.000
So,

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:01.000
what,

00:41:01.000 --> 00:41:02.000
what's the whole point?

00:41:02.000 --> 00:41:03.000
Alright.

00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:04.000
So,

00:41:04.000 --> 00:41:05.000
I give two answers

00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:06.000
in my union.

00:41:06.000 --> 00:41:07.000
One answer,

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:08.000
which I don't discuss here

00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:09.000
is that

00:41:09.000 --> 00:41:10.000
the misbah

00:41:10.000 --> 00:41:11.000
is to believe

00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:12.000
that

00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:13.000
it's God's dominion.

00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:14.000
It's not just to believe in God

00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:15.000
in abstract,

00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:16.000
but to believe that

00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:17.000
God has dominion

00:41:17.000 --> 00:41:18.000
over this

00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:19.000
world.

00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:20.000
That's right.

00:41:20.000 --> 00:41:21.000
That's the point.

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:22.000
The misbah,

00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:23.000
which is a,

00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:24.000
a Rambam concept,

00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:25.000
and that's explicit,

00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:26.000
it doesn't count as a misbah

00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:27.000
to believe in God,

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:28.000
period.

00:41:28.000 --> 00:41:29.000
You know?

00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:30.000
In a God.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:31.000
That's,

00:41:31.000 --> 00:41:32.000
for a Rambam,

00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:33.000
that means nothing.

00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:34.000
It's to believe that the God

00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:35.000
who created,

00:41:35.000 --> 00:41:36.000
blah, blah, blah,

00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:37.000
has dominion

00:41:38.000 --> 00:41:40.000
over the Earth.

00:41:41.000 --> 00:41:43.000
The point of believing in God

00:41:43.000 --> 00:41:44.000
is dominion.

00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:45.000
Right?

00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:46.000
And here you have a very,

00:41:46.000 --> 00:41:47.000
very simple idea.

00:41:47.000 --> 00:41:48.000
You see?

00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:49.000
The idea of dominion.

00:41:49.000 --> 00:41:50.000
The,

00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:51.000
the basis of the idea

00:41:51.000 --> 00:41:52.000
of dominion

00:41:52.000 --> 00:41:53.000
is in the Berakha.

00:41:53.000 --> 00:41:54.000
When you say,

00:41:54.000 --> 00:41:55.000
Melech haolam.

00:41:56.000 --> 00:41:57.000
You are

00:41:57.000 --> 00:41:58.000
the Lord,

00:41:58.000 --> 00:41:59.000
the King of the,

00:41:59.000 --> 00:42:00.000
is you have dominion

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:01.000
over the Earth.

00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:03.000
Understand?

00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:04.000
Clear?

00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:06.000
Alright?

00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:07.000
So now,

00:42:09.000 --> 00:42:10.000
there is,

00:42:10.000 --> 00:42:11.000
here,

00:42:11.000 --> 00:42:12.000
Rabi Hayan Abba Baba.

00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:13.000
Here,

00:42:13.000 --> 00:42:14.000
as you can see,

00:42:14.000 --> 00:42:15.000
to that,

00:42:15.000 --> 00:42:16.000
Rabi Hayan Abba Baba.

00:42:16.000 --> 00:42:17.000
Alright?

00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:18.000
Lame.

00:42:18.000 --> 00:42:19.000
Alright?

00:42:19.000 --> 00:42:20.000
Now,

00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:21.000
before Rabi Hayan Abba Baba,

00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:22.000
there is,

00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:23.000
in the preceding page,

00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:24.000
there is a Tanu Rabbanan.

00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:25.000
Asulol lehagam sheyeneh

00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:26.000
melech haolam hazeh

00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:27.000
bila berakha,

00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:28.000
lech haolam hazeh

00:42:28.000 --> 00:42:29.000
bila berakha ma'ad.

00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:30.000
